{"name":"Opium","hex":"#987e7e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"opium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellow-brown, addictive narcotic drug obtained from the dried juice of unripe pods of the opium poppy, Papaver somniferum, and containing alkaloids such as morphine, codeine, and papaverine.","Anything that numbs or stupefies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Opium","blocks":[{"text":"Opium is the dried latex obtained from the seed capsules of the opium poppy Papaver somniferum. Approximately 12 percent of opium is made up of the analgesic alkaloid morphine, which is processed chemically to produce heroin and other synthetic opioids for medicinal use and for the illegal drug trade. Opium's main psychoactive alkaloids, primarily morphine, act on μ-opioid receptors, causing analgesia, with long-term use leading to tolerance and dependence. The latex also contains the closely related opiates codeine and thebaine, and non-analgesic alkaloids such as papaverine and noscapine. The traditional, labor-intensive method of obtaining the latex is to scratch (\"score\") the immature seed pods (fruits) by hand; The latex leaks out and dries to a sticky yellowish residue that is later scraped off and dehydrated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Opium_pod_cut_to_demonstrate_fluid_extraction1.jpg/330px-Opium_pod_cut_to_demonstrate_fluid_extraction1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opium","wikidata":"Q46452"},{"title":"Opium (record label)","blocks":[{"text":"Opium is an American record label and rap collective founded in 2019 by American rapper Playboi Carti. The label, which is based in Atlanta, Georgia, currently holds five acts: Playboi Carti himself, rappers Ken Carson, Destroy Lonely, and ASAP Nast, and rap duo HXG, all of whom are natives to the city. The label is also affiliated with a variety of producers including KP Beatz, Lil 88, and F1lthy, who all worked extensively on Playboi Carti's second studio album, Whole Lotta Red."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opium_(record_label)","wikidata":"Q114727322"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Malwapoppy.jpg/500px-Malwapoppy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Malwapoppy.jpg/500px-Malwapoppy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poppy crop from the Malwa in India (probably Papaver somniferum var. album[1])","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalwapoppy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg/500px-Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg/1280px-Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg/500px-Minoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goddess of Ecstasy figurine from Crete, dated around the Late Bronze Age","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinoan_praying_women_archmus_Heraklion_Crete_Greece.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Een_opium_kit_op_Java._TMnr_60009390.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Een_opium_kit_op_Java._TMnr_60009390.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wiki